 a project for the enthusiastic DIYer or woodworking enthusiast. From disassembling the chair to re-gluing and re-staining the wood, you'll learn essential skills and techniques for restoring a vintage chair to its former glory. The instructions are clear and easy to follow, with accompanying photographs to guide you every step of the way. The book also includes tips and advice on choosing the right materials, protecting your work area, and troubleshooting common issues that may arise during the repair process. With this comprehensive guide, you'll be able to transform a worn-out, wobbly chair into a sturdy, beautiful piece of furniture that will last for generations to come.
The book is divided into 12 chapters, each covering a specific step in the chair repair process:
1. Preparing the workspace and materials
2. Disassembling the chair
3. Cleaning and inspecting the wood
4. Re-gluing and re-staining the wood
5. Re-building the chair frame
6. Re-attaching the seat and backrest
7. Re-assembling the chair legs
8. Adding a new finial or cap
9. Protecting the chair with varnish or polyurethane
10. Tips for maintaining and protecting your newly restored chair
11. Troubleshooting common issues
12. Conclusion and final thoughts

Throughout the book, you'll find:
• Step-by-step instructions and photographs to guide you through each task
• Information on the history and anatomy of wooden chairs, as well as tips for selecting the right type of wood for your project
• Advice on using various tools and techniques, such as hand planes, sandpaper, and clamps
• A comprehensive glossary of woodworking terms and tools
• A list of suppliers and sources for wood and other materials

Whether you're a seasoned DIYer or a complete beginner, this comprehensive guide will provide you with the skills and confidence you need to repair your own wooden